<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch minister in race for PTT job -paper.</title>
<headline>Dutch minister in race for PTT job -paper.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Minister for Economic Affairs Hans Wijers has emerged as the front runner to head the telecoms unit of post and telecoms group PTT Nederland NV, the Dutch newspaper De Telegraaf said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper, quoting sources within the company and the economic affairs ministry, said Wijers would be expected to take up the post next year and follows Dutch PTT's (KPN) decision last month to split into two separately listed units.</p>
<p>The current telecoms boss, Ben Verwaayen, has already announced his intention to leave KPN on September 1.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
